/**

@page page_peano_performance_optimisation Performance optimisation

\tableofcontents

Performance work starts from a release build, the Grid Snapshot, and an
external profiler. Logging filters keep diagnostic output from dominating
the measurement.

# Interpreting the decomposition

@ref page_peano_runtime_analysis defines the reported fields. Two values
separate common scaling limits:

- `Load Balance` measures the cell balance across the MPI ranks.
- `Rank Boundary Faces` measures the halo traffic of the rank layout.

Both are structural bounds. The time of a phase includes the work of every
dispatch, the halo waits and the memory bandwidth.

# Inter-rank imbalance

The ownership table balances cell counts at the granularity of the spawn-level
blocks and their indivisible children. A localised refined region can leave
one indivisible child heavier than the cell count a rank targets, and the
application work can be imbalanced even when the cell counts are equal.

Useful responses are:

- Increase the regular base depth when coarse partition units limit the
  balance and the extra grid fits in memory.
- Increase the global problem size so each rank receives more useful cells.
- Reduce the MPI rank count when the rank-boundary faces and the replicated
  spine dominate a small problem.

Profiles and application counters determine whether expensive particles,
limiters, source terms or local solver variants correlate with the heavy
rank.

# Dispatch cost

A phase is a fixed sequence of dispatches over the cells and the faces of the
cell connectivity. A profile dominated by the kernels points to the application
kernels; a profile dominated by the halo exchange points to the rank layout.
The local cells run while the halo messages travel, so a rank with few local
cells cannot hide its exchange.

# Adaptive mesh refinement

Refinement-plan evaluation performs integer lattice work proportional to the
request count. The substantial regrid costs are the rebuild of the tree and
the cell connectivity of the rank and the transfer of the changed cells. Oscillating refine
and erase decisions multiply this cost; stable thresholds and a suitable base
depth reduce repeated changes.

# MPI analysis

When adding ranks slows a run, compare the cells per rank, the rank-boundary
faces and the local work first. If those remain healthy, profile the halo
exchange and the collectives of the phase. Pinning can restrict the processors
visible to a rank; confirm the thread report of the runtime before
interpreting a hybrid scaling result.

*/
